{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And Rebecca was listening, etc.</b> Meaning: Scripture informs us that Rebecca was a prophetess, and was constantly listening to the words of Isaac and so forth, even though he did not speak in her presence — understand this. Therefore it says <b>And Rebecca was listening as Isaac spoke</b> and so forth, and it did not say ״וַתִּשְׁמַע רִבְקָה״ and so forth, nor did it say ״הָיְתָה שׁוֹמַעַת״ and so forth. Or perhaps it is because Isaac spoke to him secretly, and therefore he believed when Jacob came that he was Esau, for he had spoken into Esau's ear. And even though Isaac's eyes had grown dim, despite all this he informed him that these words were secret to him. Or perhaps it is for this that Scripture alluded by saying <b>and he called to Esau</b> and so forth, <b>and he said to him, My son, and he said, Here I am</b> — meaning: they secluded themselves for concealed matters."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:42.891233555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}